ence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Open seat: Neal Dunn (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Florida's 2nd District is an open Republican-held seat in the Panhandle with an R+8 lean. With Neal Dunn retiring, Austin Rogers won the GOP nomination and enters the general election with a decisive financial advantage: about $1.3 million raised, $340,000 on hand, and $1.4 million in outside support, including backing from the U.S. Chamber. Democrat Amanda Green, who has drawn support from Blue Dog groups, has raised about $348,000 with little cash remaining and no reported outside spending.\n\nRaters across the spectrum place the race at Safe or Likely Republican, with one outlet at Lean R, and prediction markets give Green roughly a 7 percent chance. No independent general-election polling is available; the only public surveys are partisan and months old. The district's fundamentals and the money gap make Rogers the clear favorite, though the open seat leaves some room for a shifting national environment to narrow the contest.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0837, "margin": -8.48}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.084, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1162, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1045, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0789, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0848, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1006, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0806, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0753, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0679, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0619, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0853, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0683, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0534, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0699, "margin": -10.0},